    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 694.962, 523.275, 748.273 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Let a general multi-interval region in d = 2 (at the line t = 0) be A = ∪Ni=1(li,ri). In a CFT the modular Hamiltonian K of the vacuum is non local except for the case of a single interval. However, it was conjectured in [9, 10] that for multi-intervals there is a local term in K having the same universal structure for any CFT. This writes"
