    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "For a general chiral field ϕ in a CFT, S. Hollands obtained a general structure of the modular evolved correlator [26]. From a clever use of the KMS condition for the modular flow and analyticity in the Euclidean plane Hollands maps the problem into a Riemann-Hilbert problem in the plane with a cut at A. His expression will be enough to get the entanglement temperatures by the limit (4.5)."
  }, {
